BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 SRJC Shone Farm Fall Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
UID:260930u9-3hLdAg0e8iSHSbY38RA
DESCRIPTION:SRJC Shone Farm welcomes the community to experience our outdo
 or learning laboratory and campus during harvest season. \n\nThis family-
 friendly event is open to the public and includes:\n\n**Animal meet and gr
 eet** *Meet the cows\, goats\, and sheep who call Shone Farm their home.*\
 n\n**U-pick pumpkins\, apples\, and sweet potatoes** *Experience the boun
 ty of the season by picking your pumpkin from our multi-acre patch. Pumpki
 ns range from small\, cute\, and petite to those humongous in size\, weigh
 ing nearly 100 lbs. Come pick apples from our orchard and sweet potatoes 
 from the field.*\n\n**Vegetable and flower farm stand** *Shop freshly pick
 ed organic produce & flower bouquets grown by SRJC students and farm inter
 ns from the Sustainable Agriculture program.*\n\n**Rotten fruit slingshot*
 * *For the young and young-at-heart\, enjoy shooting rotten fruit with our
  giant slingshot.*\n\n**Hay Rides** *Enjoy Shone Farm and the Fall season 
 by taking a hay ride around our garden and orchards.*\n\n**Tractor Show a
 nd Tell and farm equipment displays** *It takes a lot of machines to grow 
 a bountiful harvest and maintain the farm. See and learn about the tractor
 s and machinery vital to the agricultural industry.*\n\n**Professional Fal
 l Photography Station ** *Capture memories of this year's Fall Festival 
 for your holiday card by having your family's picture taken\, complimenta
 ry\, by an SRJC Applied Photography student.*\n\n**Wine tasting (21 and o
 lder)** *Taste Shone Farm wine and learn about the SRJC Wine Studies progr
 am.*\n\n**Food court & more!**\n\n**Special thanks to our sponsors:**\n\n*
 **Presenting Sponsor:*** *American Ag Credit*\n\n***Gold Sponsor:*** *The 
 Richard Kunde & Saralee McClelland Kunde Fund*\n\n***Silver Sponsors:*** *
 Bottle Barn & Western Farm Center*\n\nParking is free. This is a cashless 
 event. No dogs\, except assistance dogs\, are permitted.
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Junior College - Shone Farm
URL:https://shonefarm.santarosa.edu/shone-farm-fall-festival
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BEAT: Belew/Vai/Levin/Bozzio Performing the Music of KING CRIMSON
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
UID:261009iff8R7BQlUWhkVITUP6qqQ
DESCRIPTION:Following more than 100 acclaimed performances across North an
 d South America\, Europe\, and Japan\, BEAT returns this fall for the last
  North American tour. Former King Crimson members Adrian Belew and Tony Le
 vin are joined by guitar virtuoso Steve Vai and legendary drummer Terry Bo
 zzio to perform the music of the three landmark 1980s King Crimson albums:
  Discipline\, Beat\, and Three of a Perfect Pair. Rather than attempting t
 o recreate the original recordings\, BEAT brings this extraordinary music 
 to life with the spirit\, precision\, and adventurousness that made it so 
 enduring. Whether you've lived with these albums for decades or are discov
 ering them for the first time\, this is the final opportunity to experienc
 e one of progressive music's most celebrated catalogs performed by four of
  the best musicians on the planet.
LOCATION:Blue Note Napa Summer Sessions
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/beat-belew-vai-levin-bo
 zzio-performing-the-music-of-king-crimson/19592807/2026-10-10T20
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
