SUMMARY:Cana Ranch Uncorked: Inaugural Release Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T170000
UID:260820SP9zRIUK1Uinc0BlhV53ew
DESCRIPTION:Cana Ranch Uncorked: Inaugural Release Party\n\nSaturday\, Oct
 ober 10 | 2–5 PM Hang A Bit Ranch | 2860 Monticello Road\, Napa\, CA 945
 58 $150 Donation\n\nJoin Cana Ranch for its inaugural release party\, an i
 ntimate harvest gathering celebrating the launch of its first Napa Valley 
 Cabernet Sauvignon — and a mission to create meaningful employment oppor
 tunities for adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities \\(ID
 D\\).\n\nFounded by husband-and-wife team Tyler and Kelly Mullman\, Cana R
 anch was created with the belief that wine can be a vehicle for social imp
 act. The brand partners with organizations working to expand employment an
 d job training opportunities for adults with IDD\, with the goal of creati
 ng a sustainable path to meaningful work through the wine and hospitality 
 industries.\n\nAt Cana Ranch Uncorked\, guests will gather for an afternoo
 n of wine\, food and conversation featuring Cana Ranch winemaker Richard F
 rederick and seasonal bites thoughtfully curated by Chef Misty Phelps.\n\n
 The afternoon will include:\n\nA tasting of Cana Ranch’s inaugural 2024 
 Cabernet Sauvignon\, sourced from Tournahu Vineyard in St. Helena\n\nSelec
 t wines from Friends of Cana Ranch\n\nSeasonal bites by Chef Misty Phelps\
 n\nA silent auction\n\nRemarks from Cana Ranch founders Tyler and Kelly Mu
 llman\n\nAn introduction to the WineBev Services program and its work crea
 ting employment opportunities for adults with IDD\n\nAll proceeds from the
  event will support United Cerebral Palsy of the North Bay’s WineBev Ser
 vices program\, which provides employment and job-training opportunities f
 or adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities.\n\nCome raise 
 a glass to Cana Ranch’s first vintage and to a future where great wine c
 an help create greater opportunities for everyone.\n\n$150 donation\n\nTic
 kets & Information: https://canaranch.orderport.net/wines/events
LOCATION:Hang A Bit Ranch | 2860 Monticello Road
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/cana-ranch-uncorked-ina
 ugural-release-party/19658147/2026-10-10T14
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
