BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mighty Real: A History of LGBTQ Music: 1969-2000 with Barry Walter
 s!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
UID:2610029xXrcmhgjkuJvcn589qQJQ
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/mighty-real-a-history-of
 -lgbtq-music-1969-2000-with-barry-walters-tickets-1998864880666? Napa Prid
 e presents a deep dive into LGBTQ\\+ music history\, with world-renowned m
 usic writer Barry Walters! Plus DJ Rotten Robbie dance party! Barry Walter
 s's new book\, Mighty Real\, has earned widespread critical acclaim. He ha
 s traveled across the country to promote it\, appearing on The Kelly Clark
 son Show\, morning television programs\, popular podcasts\, and local book
 stores. Barry will read from his book\, have a Q&A\, a book signing\, then
  DJ Rotten Robbie will spin music from Barry's book for a big ol' gay danc
 e party! Barry Walters has spent 40 years documenting the intersection of 
 mainstream and LGBTQ culture. He began his career at The Village Voice —
  where he came out publicly in a 1986 Pet Shop Boys review — before beco
 ming a fixture at Spin and Rolling Stone. In 1992\, Walters’ work at the
  San Francisco Examiner made him the first critic to receive an award from
  The National Gay and Lesbian Journalists Association. Throughout the Nine
 ties\, he was The Advocate’s music columnist before a decade’s worth o
 f writing at Out. Along the way\, he’s regularly appeared in Entertainme
 nt Weekly\, NPR\, Pitchfork\, and other media mainstays. Love Me Like You 
 Should: The Brave and Bold Sylvester\, a 2020 mini-documentary he wrote an
 d co-produced for Amazon Music\, won a Clio Award. Barry's book will be av
 ailable for purchase. Event is free\, but tickets are encouraged. No-host 
 food and beverage available by our friends at Cadet.
LOCATION:Cadet Wine & Beer Bar
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2153536758873513/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
