BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Derek Irving: Rockabilly Duo\, Little Big Band\, Combo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T103000
UID:251113O1txSgSlTk2cC3t_ORhajw
DESCRIPTION:Derek Irving channels the raw\, unfiltered spirit of early roc
 k ’n’ roll\, blending the swagger of 1950s rockabilly with the driving
  rhythms of 1960s surf and rhythm & blues. The band’s sound is a nod to 
 pioneers like Chuck Berry\, Eddie Cochran\, and Carl Perkins\, but it does
 n’t stop there—there’s the grit of Bo Diddley\, the twang of Link Wr
 ay\, and a dash of reverb-soaked surf guitar straight out of a California 
 beach party.\n\nAt the heart of every show is Derek’s fiery guitar work
 —snarling riffs\, wild bends\, and rapid-fire picking that harken back t
 o rock ’n’ roll’s golden age. Anchoring the groove is the slap and t
 hump of upright bass\, a rhythmic heartbeat that gets crowds moving and ke
 eps the energy rolling from the first chord to the last encore.\n\nThis is
 n’t just a throwback—it’s a high-octane revival of the roots of rock
  ’n’ roll\, delivered with a modern edge that pulls fans of all ages o
 nto the dance floor. Whether it’s a winery crowd\, a festival stage\, or
  a late-night club\, Derek Irving and his band ignite every room with a so
 und that’s timeless\, electric\, and impossible to stand still to.
LOCATION:Downtown Novato Center
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107552137?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T000000
UID:260606lAiXVhW7HUSgafDHzc4Ecg
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market is a year-rou
 nd Saturday tradition in Sonoma County\, bringing together local farmers\,
  ranchers\, food artisans\, and neighbors from 8:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. This is
  not just a place to shop\, it's a place to connect directly with the peop
 le who grow your food. As a Slow Food Sonoma County award recipient\, the 
 market prioritizes integrity\, seasonality\, and true farm-to-community re
 lationships. Expect peak-season produce harvested just hours before market
 \, pasture-raised meats\, fresh flowers\, artisan breads\, handcrafted goo
 ds\, and thoughtfully prepared foods that reflect the region's agricultura
 l richness. Visitors can stroll the vibrant open-air market\, sample local
  flavors\, and experience Sonoma County's food culture in its most authent
 ic form. Families\, chefs\, and weekend explorers alike gather here to dis
 cover what's growing now and to support small farms that keep our local fo
 od system strong. Open every Saturday\, rain or shine\, the Santa Rosa Ori
 ginal Certified Farmers Market is a cornerstone of the community and a mus
 t-visit stop for anyone wanting to taste\, shop\, and experience Sonoma Co
 unty at its freshest.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
