BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T170000
UID:260430VdUtzT1G-kuQyYXyZ-jldA
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rainbow Book Club: Bury Your Gays by Chuck Tingle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T180000
UID:261009xcJciMKmrUiLDMx6X7eoGQ
DESCRIPTION:The Rainbow Book Club is cohosted by Mindy from Napa County Li
 brary and Napa Bookmine staff members Kass and Jules. The book club focuse
 s on books that explore and embrace queer identity. This is a free event\,
  but we appreciate your RSVP so we can plan for your attendance! We look f
 orward to welcoming you. ABOUT THE BOOK "Brilliantly bloody\, wildly fun\,
  and extremely scary\, Bury Your Gays brings a sledgehammer down on tired 
 tropes and makes a masterpiece of their guts." — Rachel Harrison\, natio
 nal bestselling author of Black Sheep “Brilliantly bloody\, wildly fun\,
  and extremely scary\, Bury Your Gays brings a sledgehammer down on tired 
 tropes and makes a masterpiece of their guts. A profoundly smart and emoti
 onally resonant novel that is sprinkled with cinema magic and a brutal Hol
 lywood reckoning.” — Rachel Harrison\, national bestselling author of 
 So Thirsty "This triumph of a book effortlessly and cleverly upends clich
 és. One of the best novels ever about LA\, the film industry\, and horror
  movies\, it delivers all the fandom\, fear\, and feels\, and then some. O
 nly Chuck Tingle can tell a story as masterfully as this\, and he once aga
 in proves that love is so real." — CJ Leede\, author of American Rapture
  The instant USA Today bestseller by Chuck Tingle about what it takes to s
 ucceed in a world that wants you dead. Named one of the Best Horror Books 
 of 2024 \\(Esquire\, Parade\, and Library Journal\\) • Winner of the Loc
 us Award for Best Horror Novel • A Lambda Literary Award finalist! • W
 inner of the 2025 Locus Award for Best Horror Novel • A Best Horror Book
  of 2024 \\(Esquire\\) • One of the Best Books of Summer 2024 \\(Esquire
 \, Paste\, HuffPost\, Publishers Weekly\\) • Winner of the 2025 Libby Aw
 ard for Best Horror • Winner of the 2025 RUSA Horror Reading List • Wi
 nner of the 2025 Dragon Award for Best Horror Novel • A CALIBA Golden Po
 ppy Award finalist • A GoodReads Choice Award finalist for Best Horror 
 • An Indie Next and LibraryReads Pick Misha knows that chasing success i
 n Hollywood can be hell. But finally\, after years of trying to make it\, 
 his big moment is here: an Oscar nomination. And the executives at the stu
 dio for his long-running streaming series know just the thing to kick his 
 career to the next level: kill off the gay characters\, "for the algorithm
 \," in the upcoming season finale. Misha refuses\, but he soon realizes th
 at he’s just put a target on his back. And what’s worse\, monsters fro
 m his horror movie days are stalking him and his friends through the hills
  above Los Angeles. Haunted by his past\, Misha must risk his entire futur
 e—before the horrors from the silver screen find a way to bury him for g
 ood. ABOUT THE AUTHOR CHUCK TINGLE is the USA Today bestselling author of 
 Camp Damascus\, Bury Your Gays\, and Straight. His books have been finalis
 ts for the Bram Stoker and CALIBA Golden Poppy Award. He is a mysterious f
 orce of energy behind sunglasses and a pink mask. He is also an anonymous 
 author of romance\, horror\, and fantasy. Tingle was born in Home of Truth
 \, Utah and now lives in Los Angeles\, California. Tingle writes to prove 
 love is real\, because love is the most important tool we have when resist
 ing the endless cosmic void. Not everything people say about Tingle is tru
 e\, but the important parts are.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1570509421459798/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
