BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Addams Family Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T220000
UID:261005jQGIP5V7gE6yRyJCV_VDzQ
DESCRIPTION:San Marin Performing Arts is kicking off the 2026–27 season 
 with The Addams Family\, a delightfully spooky musical coming to the Emily
  Gates Performing Arts Center\n\nJust in time for Halloween\, this family-
 friendly production brings the famously eccentric Addams family to the sta
 ge in a story filled with humor\, heart\, memorable music and plenty of wo
 nderfully macabre fun. In The Addams Family\, Wednesday Addams has grown u
 p—and fallen in love with a sweet\, smart young man from a perfectly “
 normal” family. When she invites him and his parents to dinner\, Wednesd
 ay asks Gomez to keep a secret from Morticia\, setting off a hilarious cha
 in of events that turns one unforgettable evening upside down.\n\nFamily f
 riendly show!\n\nOUR STUDENT CAST\n\nGomez Addams — Kaden Hockinson\n\nM
 orticia Addams — Cami Cabrera\n\nWednesday Addams — Aaliyah Ortiz\n\nP
 ugsley Addams — Rosie Chi\n\nUncle Fester — Rogan Ferrell Bell\n\nGran
 dma Addams — Lenore Schulz\n\nLurch — Wyatt Mathyssen\n\nLucas Beineke
  — Skyler Viola\n\nMal Beineke — Tobias Mossberger\n\nAlice Beineke 
 — Clara Rose\n\nThe Ancestors — Hannah Yako\, Ella Blok\, Kody Kong\, 
 Noemy Pineda Montiel\, Dasha Hirai\, Maya Geere\, Sophia Gomez
LOCATION:Emily Gates Performing Arts Center
URL:https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/the-addams-fami
 ly
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Karen Gebbia Kids Event Meet & Greet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:261005i3N2fIOSKU6hFXVGISpl2A
DESCRIPTION:Join us to celebrate Karen Gebbia's new picture book about wai
 ting patiently! And we'll be serving sweet tea as only our manager can mak
 e it\, so you won't have to wait for that!\n\nSo\, what's it about?\n\nCha
 rlotte wants to wait patiently. She really does. But waiting is hard\, esp
 ecially on a stifling Maryland morning\, when her t-shirt feels like a hot
 \, heavy blanket\, and she can't think of anything but Nana's cold\, sweet
 \, lemony\, real iced tea.\n\nThere are so many steps to Nana's secret rec
 ipe tea! Steeping\, sugaring\, cooling . . . baking muffins to go with it!
  Nana tells her to find something useful to do while she waits\, so Charlo
 tte sweeps\, and swings\, and snaps pillowcases\, but it still isn't ready
 !\n\nCharlotte has to find more things to do to pass the time\, and soon s
 he finds that a day spent waiting can be a day spent enjoying the slower m
 oments. Sometimes the sweetest things in life are the things we have to wa
 it for\, and learning to savor them slowly is a joy all its own. Included 
 is a reader's note for adults on helping kids learn how to wait and a secr
 et recipe to try at home.\n\nAuthor info!\n\nKaren Gebbia is a children's 
 book writer and naturalist based in California. Before writing for childre
 n\, Karen spent two decades writing\, publishing\, editing\, and teaching 
 scholarly writing.
LOCATION:Copperfield's Books- Petaluma
URL:https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-10-17/karen-gebbia-meet-greet
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
