BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mistah F.A.B. & Philthy Rich – Motion Detected Tour | Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T013000
UID:260922x0abwLU_E0iBIKxZTYAllw
DESCRIPTION:Two Oakland heavyweights. One stage. The Motion Detected Tour 
 hits Downtown Santa Rosa.\n\nBay Area hip-hop standouts Mistah F.A.B. and 
 Philthy Rich bring the Motion Detected Tour to Barrel Proof Lounge on Satu
 rday\, October 17 for a late-night show celebrating the sound\, history an
 d continuing evolution of Northern California rap.\n\nMISTAH F.A.B.\n\nMis
 tah F.A.B. is one of the defining voices of Oakland hip-hop and the Bay Ar
 ea's hyphy movement. Coming out of North Oakland\, F.A.B. rose alongside t
 he movement that put a new generation of Bay Area rap on the national map\
 , working with artists including Mac Dre\, E-40 and Too $hort along the wa
 y. His 2005 album Son of a Pimp and tracks including “Super Sic Wit It
 ” helped establish him as one of the era's essential artists.\n\nBut F.A
 .B.'s career reaches well beyond one era or one sound. His extensive catal
 og moves between street records\, humor\, storytelling and socially consci
 ous material\, while his work as an entrepreneur\, philanthropist and comm
 unity advocate has made him a fixture in Oakland beyond music.\n\nPHILTHY 
 RICH\n\nRepresenting East Oakland's Seminary neighborhood\, Philthy Rich h
 as built one of the most prolific catalogs in Bay Area rap. Since emerging
  in the late 2000s\, he's released a steady stream of albums\, mixtapes an
 d collaborations while taking his Oakland sound well beyond Northern Calif
 ornia.\n\nHis long list of collaborators includes E-40\, Too $hort\, Rick 
 Ross\, Lil Durk\, Young Dolph\, Gucci Mane\, Roddy Ricch\, Migos\, Lil Uzi
  Vert\, Kevin Gates\, Benny the Butcher\, 42 Dugg and Tee Grizzley\, among
  many others.\n\nNow Mistah F.A.B. and Philthy Rich hit Santa Rosa togethe
 r as the Motion Detected Tour rolls through California.\n\nThis is a chanc
 e to catch two established Oakland artists up close in the Barrel Proof sh
 owroom\, right in the heart of Downtown Santa Rosa.\n\nEVENT DETAILS\n\n 
 Saturday\, October 17\, 2026  9 PM–1:30 AM  Barrel Proof Lounge — Do
 wntown Santa Rosa  Mistah F.A.B. & Philthy Rich  Motion Detected Tour  
 $40 General Admission  21+\n\nBarrel Proof Lounge 501 Mendocino Ave Downt
 own Santa Rosa\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of
  good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/mistah-fab-philthy-rich-motion-detected-t
 our-santa-rosa-tickets-2001970668160?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rohnert Park Cotati Reuse + Repair Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T130000
UID:260921sJQie3OWAE2e26o8A57XRA
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a lamp\, small appliance\, textile\, or bike in ne
 ed of repair?\n\nBring it to the Reuse \\+ Repair Fair!‍ ‍\n\nVoluntee
 rs and specialized repair professionals will be on-hand to repair\\* your 
 items.  We ask that you stay with your item while it's being fixed\, so 
 you can learn tips for future maintenance\, how to shop for repairable goo
 ds\, and even how to repair things yourself!  \n\nIf you’d like to b
 ring an item to repair\, please register the item here: https://www.reusea
 lliance.org/rf-reg\n\n\\(Pre-registering allows us to prepare for your ite
 m!\\)\n\nThis is a free public event.\n\nThis event will also include a re
 use marketplace\, knife sharpening\, and a Clothing Swap! Bring clothing a
 nd accessories to share and take home something new-to-you. Please limit d
 onations to 1 bag per person \\(clean and good condition only\, no underga
 rments or socks please\\)\, but take as much as you’d like! More about c
 lothing swaps here.\n\n\\*We cannot guarantee your item\\(s\\) will be rep
 aired\, depending on the existing damage or breakage\, ability of voluntee
 r fixers\, and availability of materials for repair. Note: we cannot work 
 on microwaves\, repair screens on cell phones/computer devices\, or perfo
 rm any welding/brazing\, but we are happy to refer you to professionals wh
 o can. In addition\, the textile department is not able to perform the fol
 lowing:\n\nReplacing zippers\n\nRepairing shoes\, leather\, or vinyl mater
 ials\n\nPerforming alterations \\(making garments bigger/smaller\\)\n\nRep
 lacing rivets/grommets\n\nHemming certain fabrics \\(stretchy fabric\, sle
 ek/luxury fabrics e.g. prom dresses\\)\n\nIf you are in need of garment he
 mming\, we require that you please pin your garment to the desired length 
 before you arrive.\n\nJoin Us!\n\nDo you enjoy fixing things?  Or want to
  help out in other ways?  We need you! Sign up here: https://www.reuseall
 iance.org/rf-volunteer\n\nor email volunteer@reusealliance.org if you have
  any questions.
LOCATION:Rohnert Park Community Center
URL:https://www.reusealliance.org/events/rohnert-park-cotati-reuse-repair-
 fair
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
