DESCRIPTION:Wednesdays Weekly · 8 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nOctober 7 – D
 ecember 2\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nExceptions\n\nNo class Novembe
 r 11\, Veterans Day\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\
 n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\, Handcrafted for the Holidays\n\nExperienc
 e Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$265\n\nMa
 terials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nThis 8 week ses
 sion with our pottery texture queen\, Lynn Wood\, will be slab based with 
 focus on the holidays. The projects will center around creating forms for
  celebrating including serving dishes\, decorative surfaces\, holiday the
 med gifts and more. This class will help you get started early and be pr
 epared for gift giving and holiday success. Everyone will learn to make a 
 new lantern. Fun and laughs will also be included.\n\nInterested in spendi
 ng a bit more time in the studio with Lynn Wood? This session\, opt-in for
  and additional 1.5 hours of guided working time each class session in the
  studio with Lynn Wood for an extra fee. Regularly scheduled class will oc
 cur from 10am-1pm\, and then our additional Guided Working Session with Ly
 nn Wood will run from 1:30pm-3:00pm
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/handbuilding-here-comes-the
 -holidays/
