DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
UID:2610095bmohNghqUWJzd-XsARkqg
DESCRIPTION:HALLOWINE WALK\n\nTrick\, Treat\, & Taste in Yountville\n\nSat
 urday\, October 24\, 2026 12:00 – 4:00 p.m. Washington St. | Yountville\
 n\nCelebrate Halloween with a spirited afternoon in the heart of Yountvill
 e!\n\nJoin us for the inaugural Hallowine Walk: Trick\, Treat & Taste in Y
 ountville\, where wine\, Halloween\, and small-town charm come together fo
 r a one-of-a-kind fall experience.\n\nYour ticket includes a commemorative
  wine cup\, event wristband\, and tasting map. After checking in at Vetera
 ns Memorial Park\, you’ll stroll through Yountville\, visiting participa
 ting wineries\, tasting rooms\, restaurants\, and local businesses while e
 njoying wine tastings\, festive décor\, seasonal surprises\, and exclusiv
 e event-day offerings. \n\nCostumes are encouraged\, so gather your frien
 ds\, dress in your Halloween best\, and enjoy an unforgettable afternoon o
 f wine\, treats\, and festive fun!\n\nTicket Includes:\n\nHallowine Walk c
 up\n\nWine tastings at participating locations\n\nEvent wristband and tast
 ing map\n\nAccess to exclusive event-day specials and promotions\n\nA fest
 ive afternoon exploring downtown Yountville\n\nCheers to a hauntingly good
  time—we can’t wait to see you there!\n\nMust be 21\\+ to participate.
LOCATION:Town of Yountville
URL:https://yountville.com/hallowine-walk/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sing Napa Valley presents “American Songbook Singer Showcase”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T170000
UID:261008p0Z-587DBkCNdP_WyQsbng
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s musical heritage with Sing Napa Valley a
 t the *American Songbook Singer Showcase*. Presented in honor of the Unite
 d States’ 250th anniversary\, this lively afternoon concert travels from
  the 1920s through the early 1960s with jazz standards\, Broadway favorite
 s\, and memorable songs from film. Two concerts: Saturday\, October 24 & S
 unday\, October 25 at 3pm.\n\nWhether these classics are lifelong favorite
 s or brand-new discoveries\, *American Songbook Singer Showcase* promises 
 an uplifting celebration of music’s power to bridge generations and brin
 g people together.\n\nEnjoy timeless music by George and Ira Gershwin\, Co
 le Porter\, Hoagy Carmichael\, and Irving Berlin\, including favorites suc
 h as “Mr. Sandman\,” “Honeysuckle Rose\,” “Night and Day\,” an
 d “Dream a Little Dream of Me.” Sing Napa Valley choir members and spe
 cial guests will take the spotlight in solos\, duets\, trios\, and small e
 nsembles\, joined by collaborative pianist Anthony Mayor. Bring family and
  friends for an uplifting celebration of music that connects generations.
LOCATION:American Legion Hall
URL:http://www.singnapavalley.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
