SUMMARY:Healthy Hearty Meal Prep with Erin Shallat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T120000
UID:261005gdhATRSOS0esU9vSNXbg2w
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, October 5\, 2026 10:00 am to 12:00 pm\n\nWeekly on Mo
 ndays\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Art
 s\, Wellness\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\n
 Registration Cost:\n\n$25\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registrat
 ion Cost:\n\n$25\n\nAs the founder of Erin Shallat Catering in San Francis
 co\, Erin brings over two decades of experience in transforming nutrition 
 into an art form. Her unique approach intertwines advanced studies in nutr
 ition with a deep passion for the culinary arts. Erin’s goal is to make 
 meal prep approachable and not intimidating for everyone\, encouraging stu
 dents to gain confidence in the kitchen. She believes in working with seas
 onal produce and what’s available\, helping students learn to create hea
 lth-conscious yet tantalizing menus that embrace both flavor and wellness.
  Introducing our Fall/Winter Cooking Series—designed for both returning 
 and new students. This six-week program runs Mondays and Wednesdays\, each
  with a unique focus to offer variety\, skill-building\, and fun throughou
 t the season.Every Monday\, students will dive into healthy\, hearty meal 
 prep sessions. Each class focuses on creating nutritious\, satisfying dish
 es that can be portioned out and taken home—perfect for fueling the week
  ahead. These hands-on sessions ensure participants leave with ready-to-ea
 t meals and new confidence in their culinary skills.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/healthy-hearty-meal-prep-wi
 th-erin-shallat/2026-10-05/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T194500
UID:261001YcfqK7UTc0qX2tddC0c72Q
DESCRIPTION:Bring a flashlight and your sense of wonder as you e
 xplore the park after dark. This hike heads up to the summit o
 f Bald Mountain\, where we will see the moon rise over the May
 acamas and the sun set over Sonoma Valley. This is a strenuous
  hike of approximately 6.5 miles with 1500+ of vertical and som
 e steep sections (not recommended for children under 12).\n\n**Mee
 t at the main parking lot at least 10 minutes prior to the st
 art time**. Advance registration is $10 for general admission\, o
 r $5 for youth (12-17 year olds)\, students\, Sugarloaf members\,
  Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers. All minors must be accompanied by
  a parent or legal guardian. **You must register on this page 
 to attend\; tickets on site are $15** (exact change only) **and m
 ight not be available.** Bring your **flashlight**\, **at least 3
 2oz of water**\, **snacks**\, and **extra layers for the evening*
 *. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/oct2026moon-bald
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
