 hat love brought them together forging a friendship with their shared pass
 ion at the center. Together\, these three friends bring an unforgettable n
 ight of music sure to delight any audience. $17 advance AT THE DOOR $22 \\
 *The price includes a $2 ticketing fee per ticket to cover costs of 3rd pa
 rty ticket service and credit card fees. Doors open 6:30.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/946142651388965/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alibi October Book Club: Her Body and Other Parties by Carmen Mari
 a Machado
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T190000
UID:261003r-F_mwOZV02zF22Bpv9LBw
DESCRIPTION:Just in time for Halloween\, we'll be reading Carmen Maria Mac
 hado's "Her Body and Other Parties" and discussing it Thursday\, October 2
 9th at 7pm. Finalist for the National Book Award for Fiction “\\[These s
 tories\\] vibrate with originality\, queerness\, sensuality and the strang
 e.”—Roxane Gay “In these formally brilliant and emotionally charged 
 tales\, Machado gives literal shape to women’s memories and hunger and d
 esire. I couldn’t put it down.”—Karen Russell In Her Body and Other 
 Parties\, Carmen Maria Machado blithely demolishes the arbitrary borders b
 etween psychological realism and science fiction\, comedy and horror\, fan
 tasy and fabulism. While her work has earned her comparisons to Karen Russ
 ell and Kelly Link\, she has a voice that is all her own. In this electric
  and provocative debut\, Machado bends genre to shape startling narratives
  that map the realities of women’s lives and the violence visited upon t
 heir bodies. A wife refuses her husband’s entreaties to remove the green
  ribbon from around her neck. A woman recounts her sexual encounters as a 
 plague slowly consumes humanity. A salesclerk in a mall makes a horrifying
  discovery within the seams of the store’s prom dresses. One woman’s s
 urgery-induced weight loss results in an unwanted houseguest. And in the b
 ravura novella “Especially Heinous\,” Machado reimagines every episode
  of Law & Order: Special Victims Unit\, a show we naïvely assumed had sho
 wn it all\, generating a phantasmagoric police procedural full of doppelg
 ängers\, ghosts\, and girls with bells for eyes. Earthy and otherworldly\
 , antic and sexy\, queer and caustic\, comic and deadly serious\, Her Body
  and Other Parties swings from horrific violence to the most exquisite sen
 timent. In their explosive originality\, these stories enlarge the possibi
 lities of contemporary fiction. Books are available in the shop\, online a
 nd ebook at bookshop.org/shop/alibibookshop and audio: libro.fm/alibibooks
 hop
LOCATION:Anchor Pantry
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1803503417501630/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Schnucks Wine Dinner with Jeff Bundschu
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T210000
UID:260824hx0e58aN6ES2hlgcZDhpPg
DESCRIPTION:Schnucks Wine Dinner with Jeff Bundschu\n\nWe invite you to jo
 in Jeff Bundschu at Schnucks Des Peres in St. Louis MO on Wednesday Octobe
 r 28th from 6-9pm for a special wine dinner. It will be a culinary experie
 nce you won’t want to miss\, delicately paired with exceptional wines an
 d their friendly staff.\n\nFROM THE HOST\n\nJoin us for an exclusive five-
 course culinary journey featuring the exceptional cool-climate estate wine
 s of Gundlach Bundschu\, Sonoma’s oldest continuously family-owned winer
 y. The evening features sixth-generation vintner and special guest Jeff Bu
 ndschu\, who will share his personal stories\, deep-rooted passion\, and d
 istinctively vibrant approach to California winemaking. As each meticulous
 ly paired course unfolds\, you will gain firsthand insight into the unique
  terroir of their historic Rhinefarm estate\, their sustainable wine-growi
 ng philosophies\, and the meticulous crafting process that has defined the
  Bundschu family legacy for nearly 170 years.\n\nMENU\n\nGreeter: Gundlach
  Bundschu 2025 Gewurztraminer | Gundlach Bundschu 2025 Sauvignon Blanc \\}
  Goat Cheese Tart with Asian Pear and Star Fruit | Gundlach Bundschu 2024 
 Chardonnay \\} Seared Scallops with Green Apple Beurre Blanc | GunBun Pino
 t Noir 2022 \\} Smoked Turkey Roulade with Wild Rice | Gundlach Bundschu M
 ountain Cuvee 2023 \\} Cocoa Rubbed Rack of Lamb with Plum Reduction\, Swe
 et Potato Puree and Haricot Vert | Gundlach Bundschu 2021 Cabernet Sauvign
 on \\} Basque Chocolate Cheesecake with Blackberries\n\nCan’t make it? P
 lease share with your local foodies!\n\nBOOK NOW
LOCATION:Gundland Bundschu Winery
URL:https://www.gunbun.com/event/schnucks-wine-dinner/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
