BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adding Beauty and Interest to Your Garden with California Native P
 lants
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T130000
UID:260930Xma2vwbBV0yEkJBz5Sml1w
DESCRIPTION:There are many wonderful California native shrubs and perennia
 ls that make perfect additions to existing gardens and are great replaceme
 nts for non-native plants. And because they are native to this climate\, t
 hey are better able to withstand the swings in rainfall and temperature we
  are seeing more frequently.\n\nMaster Gardener Linda King will discuss so
 me reasons for adding California native plants to your garden\, and recomm
 end a variety of native plants that are easy to care for and make great ad
 ditions to any existing garden. Join us under the shade of the trees at Pe
 taluma Bounty Unity Garden. There will be a period for answering all your 
 questions.
LOCATION:Petaluma Bounty
URL:https://ucanr.edu/site/mg-sonoma
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T173000
UID:260831bhjbeMY7ukq2tmFq-W7GcQ
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kenny Washington At Sebastiani Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
UID:260728-TWqBbfyPkGmKNmnrv8p8Q
DESCRIPTION:A Night with One of Jazz’s Most Celebrated Vocalists\n\nGet 
 ready for an unforgettable evening as we welcome the extraordinary **Kenny
  Washington**\, a vocalist whose range\, warmth\, and storytelling have ma
 de him one of the most revered voices in jazz today.\n\nWith a style that 
 blends the soul of the great jazz crooners with the precision of a master 
 musician\, Kenny brings every song to life—swinging effortlessly\, soari
 ng through impossibly agile lines\, and delivering ballads with heart‑st
 opping beauty. His performances are intimate\, joyful\, and deeply human.\
 n\nThis is a rare chance to experience a world‑class jazz vocalist in an
  intimate Sonoma setting. Whether you’re a longtime fan or discovering h
 im for the first time\, Kenny Washington’s voice will stay with you long
  after the final note.
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theater
URL:http://www.sonomavalleyjazzsociety.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T143000
UID:2606262qX-7vqhk0-UksUKuyHJ4g
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\nWhite Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil\n\nSusa
 nna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\nB
 liss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nHeirl
 oom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\nSmoked Bacon-Grain Mustard D
 ressing\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian Seven-
 Spiced Chicken Breast\n\nIndonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable Ragout
 \, Balado Sauce\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Vanilla Bur
 nt Basque Cheesecake\n\nRaspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licorice-Poache
 d Cherries\n\nBrown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime\n\nEstate Ingredien
 ts:\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, Lemons\, Olive Oi
 l\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tomatoes\, Zucchini
  and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservations are require
 d. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
