BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
UID:261004dSTZjS2OlEWpx7LF7lQ5nA
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
UID:260930F-go9WXRi0-VIeXOcXr2WA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two ofrendas in the House of Happy Walls Museum from Oc
 t. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tradi
 tion that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spani
 sh for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the memor
 y of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and adve
 nturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected to 
 the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, traditi
 onal elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, th
 e installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing and 
 travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, and 
 the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared\,
  participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\, 
 and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\, 
 drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a be
 loved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more peop
 le participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitors 
 who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or e
 ven a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Tai Chi Flow Winter 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T100000
UID:260929tlDzmf746kGFOTJQspekwg
DESCRIPTION:Embrace the tranquility of winter Sunday mornings at S
 ugarloaf as our experienced instructor\, Diana Latorre\, guides yo
 u in the ancient practice of Tai Chi every first and third Sun
 day of the month. This gentle holistic wellness practice is perf
 ect for beginners and those with limited mobility\, as the pract
 ice can be done seated. Not recommended for children under 16 y
 ears old.\n\nTickets are $15 or free with a September 2026 or n
 ewer Park Rx from a Sonoma County Medical Provider. Click here 
 for Park Rx information. To sign up with a Park Rx\, please em
 ail the signed Rx form to alma@sonomaecologycenter.org. Please hav
 e your Rx available at the time of sign-up\, as the number of
  Park Rx tickets is limited and you will be asked to turn in
  a copy at the time of registration. Wear layers\, comfortable 
 footwear\, bring water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snac
 k or a picnic to enjoy after the event. Parking fees apply. He
 avy rains cancel.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026taichi
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunday Sessions in The Lounge – DJs\, Dancing & Requests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T230000
UID:2609291evx8JhpCEybdYYdSSPjKw
DESCRIPTION:SUNDAY SESSIONS IN THE LOUNGE ROTATING DJs • OPEN FORMAT •
  REQUESTS WELCOME • NO COVER\n\nSunday nights have a new home in The Lou
 nge at Barrel Proof.\n\nEvery Sunday at 8 PM\, a rotating lineup of DJs ta
 kes over the front room for Sunday Sessions — an open-format dance party
  where the playlist isn't locked into one genre and requests are part of t
 he fun.\n\nOpen format means the DJ gets to read the room. One song might 
 take you back\, the next might be something you were blasting in the car t
 his week. Different genres\, different eras and different DJs from week to
  week\, with plenty of room for the crowd to help steer the night.\n\nGot 
 a song you want to hear? Ask the DJ.\n\nAnd there's more happening under t
 he same roof. Start your evening with Sunday Funday Comedy at 6 PM\, then 
 at 8 PM Barrel Proof gives you two ways to keep the night going:\n\n THE 
 LOUNGE — 8 PM Sunday Sessions Rotating DJs • Open Format • Requests 
 • Dancing\n\n MAIN ROOM — 8 PM Sunday Night Karaoke Grab the mic and 
 sing on the big stage.\n\nDance in the Lounge\, sing in the Main Room\, or
  bounce between the two all night.\n\nEvery Sunday • 8 PM Barrel Proof L
 ounge 501 Mendocino Ave • Downtown Santa Rosa 21+ • No Cover\n\nCheck 
 out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/sunday-sessions-in-the-lounge-djs-dancing
 -requests-tickets-2002178174818?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
