BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa Beginner - 4-Week Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
UID:261003iWcPMQGNqUKgLYKCLZjCKQ
DESCRIPTION:Cuban Salsa Class with Eric Celestino & Abigail Celestino\n\n4
 week class\n\nNovember 5- November 26\n\nClass requires a minimum of 8 reg
 istrations to run. Please register soon so we can secure the session!\n\nT
 his is a beginner cuban salsa—you will learn your basic footwork and tur
 ns.\n\nIn this class\, you will learn the fundamentals of Cuban Salsa\, in
 cluding body movement\, rhythm\, musicality\, footwork\, partner connectio
 n\, and partnerwork patterns inspired by authentic Cuban dance culture. We
  focus on proper technique\, coordination\, flow\, and natural body expres
 sion\, while also building confidence and strong foundations.\n\nClasses a
 re structured with:\n\n• Warm-up and body movement\n\n• Footwork and r
 hythm exercises\n\n• Partnerwork technique\n\n• Short combinations and
  practical applications\n\nOur goal is to help you understand how to dance
  salsa\, not just memorize steps — developing timing\, connection\, and 
 a comfortable\, joyful way of dancing.\n\nCome dance with us\, grow your t
 echnique\, and experience the energy and flavor of Cuba in a supportive an
 d welcoming environment.\n\nBook your spot\n\nDate & Time:\n\n4week class\
 , November 5- November 26\n\nThursdays @ 7:30 PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood 
 Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor m
 arking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mushroom Architect- Chris Maurer- North by North Coast Fall Lectur
 e
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
UID:260925h688WcCnqU2mXd9IfHJL0Q
DESCRIPTION:What if we could grow the materials we build with? Join AIA Re
 dwood Empire for an evening with architect Chris Maurer\, founder of redho
 use studio\, as he explores how mycelium\, the root-like network of mushro
 oms\, can become a building material. From NASA-supported research into sp
 ace habitats to his Mycohab initiative in Namibia\, Maurer’s work offers
  a look at how architecture can turn waste into useful materials and reduc
 e its environmental impact. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Lavish Experience Center
URL:https://aiare.org/events/save-the-date-north-by-north-coast-fall-lectu
 re-featuring-chris-maurer/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BLS Certification Class (American Heart Association)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T090000
UID:260918XH1rwbVAV0uFIH_-4XK8dA
DESCRIPTION:BLS Certification Class \\(AHA\\) - In Person\, Instructor-Led
 \n\nAmerican Heart Association BLS certification class \\(in-person\, inst
 ructor-led class in our Rohnert Park classroom\\). BLS \\(Basic Life Suppo
 rt\\) is the required CPR class for healthcare providers. Includes cardiac
  and respiratory arrest management\, CPR\, AED use\, and choking treatment
  for all ages. This class is appropriate for initial BLS or BLS renewal.\n
 \nVive CPR is an American Heart Association \\(AHA\\) Training Site. AHA "
 BLS Provider" certifications are issued on the same day.\n\nWe also offer 
 Blended Learning BLS certification courses \\(online course plus in-person
  Skills Session\\).\n\nLearn from a top-rated\, local CPR training company
